# OWL 2 RL application-oriented extensions for Eyeling.
#
# These rules are intentionally kept separate from owl2rl-eyeling.n3 because
# they are not part of the published OWL 2 RL/RDF rule table.  They are sound
# OWL semantic consequences for finite, materialization-oriented applications:
# a known property value proves membership in the corresponding cardinality-1
# restriction.  In OWL 2 DL terms, minCardinality 1 is equivalent to an
# existential/someValuesFrom restriction over owl:Thing, and qualified
# minQualifiedCardinality 1 is equivalent to someValuesFrom over the qualifier.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

{ ?r owl:minCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
  ?r owl:onProperty ?p .
  ?u ?p ?v . }
=> { ?u rdf:type ?r . } .

{ ?r owl:minQualifiedCardinality "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
  ?r owl:onProperty ?p .
  ?r owl:onClass ?c .
  ?u ?p ?v .
  ?v rdf:type ?c . }
=> { ?u rdf:type ?r . } .